schema Resource
generation control-1
authority native-kernel
absorbs 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/actors.py
absorbs 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/provider_state.py
absorbs 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/resource_admission.py
note one identity substrate; Actor Relationship Provider Admission are components

field resource_id
  type text
  role identity
  required true

field components
  type list
  values actor institution relationship evidence opportunity repository communication contribution provider capacity

field authority
  type enum
  values verified asserted inferred
  default asserted
  note provenance is mandatory; a model guess never reads as a fact

field provenance
  type text
  required true

component ActorComponent
  field display_name text
  field node_kind enum organization person publication program
  field role text
  field org_id text

component RelationshipComponent
  edge_kinds employs authority_over evidence_for funds publishes_in contact_of opportunity_unlock
  invariant edge-meaning-is-typed
    statement edges sharing a from relation to shape are not interchangeable
    derived-from operating-model law 2

component ProviderComponent
  derivation fold-over-occurrences
  states ready cooling capacity_exhausted manual_pause
  invariant hard-capacity-dominates
    statement a transient observation never shortens a stated hard-capacity window
    derived-from run6 codex relaunch at 22:43 into a window resetting Aug 19
  invariant success-does-not-clear-capacity
    statement one served response is not evidence that capacity returned

component CapacityComponent
  field protected_floor_bytes u64
  field per_plane_quota_bytes u64
  field max_grant_bytes u64
  invariant grants-are-subtracted
    statement concurrent claimants never see the same free bytes twice
    derived-from run6 five planes and ENOSPC
  invariant admission-precedes-work
    statement footprint is compared against headroom before work starts
  invariant stale-grants-age-out
    statement a grant from a killed holder is reclaimed on a deadline

verdicts admit defer reject
  note defer means waiting could help; reject means it could not
